  "descriptionEmployeur": "<h2>Who we are</h2>\n<h3>And why it matters</h3>\n<p>We are a leading Belgian CRO based in Thuin, supporting pharmaceutical companies with analytical services that meet EMA and FDA standards. With 280 experts and cutting-edge technologies, we combine scientific excellence with human values to accelerate access to life-changing therapies.</p>\n<p></p>",
  "descriptionJob": "<h2>Your next challenge</h2>\n<h3>Ready to make a difference? Here's what awaits you.</h3>\n<p>As a Laboratory Analyst in one of our HPLC teams, you&rsquo;ll play a vital role in ensuring the quality and safety of medicines that will improve patients&rsquo; lives worldwide. Working at the heart of drug development, you&rsquo;ll contribute to projects from early stages through clinical and commercial phases, helping therapies reach those who need them faster.</p>\n<h2></h2>\n<h2></h2>\n<h2>Your key responsibilities</h2>\n<h3>Here's what you will be in charge of:</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Performing HPLC analyses using validated methods</li>\n<li>Preparing samples and conducting analyses using state-of-the art laboratory equipment</li>\n<li>Carrying out physico-chemical tests such as Karl Fischer, UV spectroscopy, pH, osmolality, CCIT and particle counting</li>\n<li>Writing stability reports and certificates of analysis</li>\n<li>Applying pharmacopoeial requirements and regulatory standards in daily activities</li>\n<li>Working closely with the Technical Leader and HPLC team</li>\n</ul>\n<p></p>",
