  "niveauEtude": "<h2>Skills you'll need to bring</h2>\n<p>To succeed in this role, you'll demonstrate:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Bachelor&rsquo;s (or Master's) degree in a scientific field such as chemistry or agronomy, or equivalent experience</li>\n<li>Hands-on experience or internship in HPLC in a regulated environment, (ideally, GxP)</li>\n<li>Practical and theoretical knowledge of physico-chemical tests including KF and pH</li>\n<li>Fluency in French</li>\n<li>English proficiency at A2&ndash;B1 level</li>\n<li>Strong organisational skills and attention to detail</li>\n<li>A collaborative mindset and ease working within a small scientific team</li>\n</ul>\n<p></p>",
  "benefitsComments": "<p></p>\n<h2>Our commitment to you</h2>\n<p>We believe your growth matters as much as your contribution. From day one, you&rsquo;ll benefit from a tailored onboarding programme and continuous learning opportunities. You&rsquo;ll enjoy a competitive salary package with extra-legal benefits, plus a work culture that values respect and collaboration.</p>\n<p>Here's why you'll love working with us.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>A stable work environment</li>\n<li>Comprehensive training to boost your expertise</li>\n<li>Working conditions that ensures work-life balance</li>\n<li>Meaningful projects with public health impact</li>\n</ul>\n<p></p>",
